            // is used. But we need the contract's randomness to match our loop's win condition.
            // We can't control block.timestamp exactly, but we can loop and call play;
            // after a win, the pot should be 0 in the reference and >0 in the mutant.
            // We just call play and check the invariant after each call.
            vm.prank(player);
            c.play{value: 10}();
        }
        // Invariant: pot is always 0 in the reference, but in the mutant it will be >0 after a win.
        // Actually, the reference pot is 0 after a win, but could be >0 if no win yet. So the
        // invariant is: if a win has occurred, pot == 0 in reference. The mutant will have pot > 0.
