        // Simpler: after a win, pot becomes 0. We don't know if it was a win unless we observe pot==0.
        // But we can check the general rule: it's impossible for pot to be 10 after a play when the reference
        // contract resets it to 0 on a win, because a win always empties the pot.
        // However, the fuzzer may hit a non-win (random==1) where pot==10. To create a rule that always holds
